        <headline>Flood Advisory issued September 25 at 8:12AM CDT until September 25 at 11:15AM CDT by NWS Amarillo TX</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Urban area and small stream flooding caused by excessive
rainfall is expected.

* WHERE...Western Armstrong County in the panhandle of Texas...
Carson County in the panhandle of Texas...
Deaf Smith County in the panhandle of Texas...
Southeastern Oldham County in the panhandle of Texas...
Southern Potter County in the panhandle of Texas...
Randall County in the panhandle of Texas...

* WHEN...Until 1115 AM CDT.

* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 812 AM CDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to
thunderstorms. This  is causing urban and small stream flooding.
Between 1 and 3 inches of rain have fallen.
- Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are expected over the
area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Amarillo, Hereford, Canyon, Panhandle, Claude, White Deer, Lake
Tanglewood, Skellytown, Mescalero Park, Bushland, Umbarger, Palo
Duro Canyon, Buffalo Lake, Dawn, Wildorado, Washburn, Wayside,
Simms, Bootleg and Timbercreek Canyon.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood
</description>
        <instruction>Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.</instruction>
